{"file":"keelson-0.4.0-v2.zip","bytes":186373,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"keelson","description":"Establish a disciplined, issue-driven agentic operating model in any repo, against any tracker (GitHub, GitLab, Jira, Linear, or any API/CLI/MCP). The adopt-keelson skill interviews you and writes a tracker-agnostic AGENTS.md plus a selectable lifecycle skill-pack; the tune-gates skill establishes or refines the quality gates standalone.","version":"0.4.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/innovestrum/keelson","homepage":"https://github.com/innovestrum/keelson","keywords":["agentic-workflow","issue-driven","tracker-agnostic","agents-md","skills","github","gitlab","jira","linear","codex","claude-code"]}],"skills":[{"path":".agents/skills/adopt-keelson/SKILL.md","name":"adopt-keelson","description":"Adopt keelson''s issue-driven agentic operating model in this repo. Runs a deliberate, multi-round interview (≈8–20 rounds: it maps your SDLC, then makes you decide each pillar), then writes a tracker-agnostic client AGENTS.md plus the selected lifecycle skills — provider-neutral across GitHub, GitLab, Jira, Linear, or any API/CLI/MCP. The gate pillar defers to the tune-gates skill (run it standalone later to add/tune a gate). Trigger on \"adopt keelson\", \"set up the agentic workflow\", \"establish the issue-driven flow\", or a repo that wants an AGENTS.md.","headings":["Adopt keelson","1 · How to run the interview","2 · The rounds","3 · Placeholders (the only things you fill)","4 · Fill & write","5 · Verify & hand back","Gotchas"],"name_hint":"adopt · keelson"},{"path":".agents/skills/tune-gates/SKILL.md","name":"tune-gates","description":"Establish or refine a repo's quality gates **independently of the full adopt-keelson interview** — both the CI quality-gate policy (which checks block merge) and the verification gates (review, source-change, source-sync, parity). Runs in ≈2–4 rounds, is re-runnable to add/tune/drop a gate on a repo that already adopted keelson, and is the canonical gate spec adopt-keelson defers to. Trigger on \"set up the quality gates\", \"add a gate\", \"tune the gates\", \"refine the verification gates\".","headings":["Tune gates","1 · Orient & pick the mode","2 · Read the repo shape (drives which gates fit)","3 · The rounds","4 · Fill & write","5 · Verify & hand back","Gotchas"],"name_hint":"tune · gates"},{"path":"skills/adopt-keelson/SKILL.md","name":"adopt-keelson","description":"Adopt keelson''s issue-driven agentic operating model in this repo. Runs a deliberate, multi-round interview (≈8–20 rounds: it maps your SDLC, then makes you decide each pillar), then writes a tracker-agnostic client AGENTS.md plus the selected lifecycle skills — provider-neutral across GitHub, GitLab, Jira, Linear, or any API/CLI/MCP. The gate pillar defers to the tune-gates skill (run it standalone later to add/tune a gate). Trigger on \"adopt keelson\", \"set up the agentic workflow\", \"establish the issue-driven flow\", or a repo that wants an AGENTS.md.","headings":["Adopt keelson","1 · How to run the interview","2 · The rounds","3 · Placeholders (the only things you fill)","4 · Fill & write","5 · Verify & hand back","Gotchas"],"name_hint":"adopt · keelson"},{"path":"skills/tune-gates/SKILL.md","name":"tune-gates","description":"Establish or refine a repo's quality gates **independently of the full adopt-keelson interview** — both the CI quality-gate policy (which checks block merge) and the verification gates (review, source-change, source-sync, parity). Runs in ≈2–4 rounds, is re-runnable to add/tune/drop a gate on a repo that already adopted keelson, and is the canonical gate spec adopt-keelson defers to. Trigger on \"set up the quality gates\", \"add a gate\", \"tune the gates\", \"refine the verification gates\".","headings":["Tune gates","1 · Orient & pick the mode","2 · Read the repo shape (drives which gates fit)","3 · The rounds","4 · Fill & write","5 · Verify